  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to be deep-fried; to come out crispy",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to be deep-fried; to come out (well) fried",
      "explanation": "For food being deep-fried to finish cooking, especially with a desirably crisp result. The intransitive partner of {揚|あ}げる."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28726_agaru_ex1",
      "japanese": "⟦{天|てん}ぷら→天ぷら：04948_tenpura⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧カラッ⟦と→と：00512_to⟧{揚|あ}がった。",
      "english": "The tempura came out crispy.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28726_agaru_ex2",
      "japanese": "⟦{油|あぶら}→油：01693_abura⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{温度|おんど}→温度：00333_ondo⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦{高|たか}い→高い：00500_takai⟧⟦と→と：00512_to⟧、⟦すぐ→すぐ：00814_sugu⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{揚|あ}がる。",
      "english": "If the oil temperature is high, things fry quickly.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28726_agaru_ex3",
      "japanese": "⟦{衣|ころも}→衣：14162_koromo⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧きつね⟦{色|いろ}→色：00849_iro⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{揚|あ}がったら⟦{油|あぶら}→油：01693_abura⟧⟦から→から：00504_kara⟧⟦{取|と}り{出|だ}して→取り出す：04220_toridasu⟧⟦ください→ください：02899_kudasai⟧。",
      "english": "Once the batter has fried to a golden brown, take it out of the oil.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Intransitive verb describing food finishing the deep-frying process. Often paired with adverbs that describe the texture or color of the result.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- カラッ⟦と→と：00512_to⟧{揚|あ}がる: to fry up crispy\n- きつね⟦{色|いろ}→色：00849_iro⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{揚|あ}がる: to fry to a golden brown\n- ⟦うまく→うまい：01279_umai⟧{揚|あ}がる: to come out well\n\nWATCH OUT:\n- ⟦{上|あ}がる→上がる：00615_agaru⟧ (00615): to go up — the most common ⟦あがる→あがる：17309_agaru⟧\n- ⟦あがる→あがる：17309_agaru⟧ (17309): to be nervous; to lose one's composure\n\nTRANSITIVE PAIR:\n- ⟦{揚|あ}げる→揚げる：16879_ageru⟧: to deep-fry — used when the cook is the focus",
